)\".\n\n**Auth:** Required — bearer API key via `Authorization: Bearer <key>` header, or a cookie session from the dashboard. Org-scoped keys can add an `X-Project-Id` header to target a project.\n\n**Request body (JSON, required):**\n- `fields` (required) — an object of string key/value pairs holding the \"Credential fields required by the app\" (e.g., `api_key: sk-...`)\n- `connectionId` (optional) — used to \"Reconnect an existing connection\"\n\n**Responses:** `200` returns `{ success: boolean }`; `400` returns an error object for a \"Validation error or provider not available\".\n\n**Programmatic credential setup:** Yes — this endpoint exists precisely for connecting apps with direct credentials (API keys, service accounts) instead of OAuth. So a provider credential such as an Anthropic API key could be set via this call, assuming that provider is supported.\n\n**Per-agent scoping:** Not via this endpoint — connections here are scoped to the project/organization, and there's no agent parameter in the path or body. However, the spec's tag list mentions an Agents section for managing \"agents and their access tokens, secrets, and configuration,\" suggesting agent-level credentials may exist elsewhere in the API. The full documentation index at `https://onecli.sh/docs/llms.txt` would clarify that.","durationMs":14081,"url":"https://onecli.sh/docs/api-reference/apps/connect-app-with-credentials.md"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7395fd08-5d50-4576-8394-bb92ada7b3ba","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/workspace/agent","sessionId":"0bec9074-f0ee-4108-82bf-5bb584ae73da","version":"2.1.197","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"polished-jumping-turing"}
